<div id="2026-11-12-ai2-supergrok-quota-and-page-debug" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-11-12 — AI2: SuperGrok is its own allowance; page questions get curated source; source reads are gate-enforced</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Three changes in the AI2 path. (1) <em>Routing.</em> An exhausted OpenRouter daily cap no longer disqualifies SuperGrok — its own guard and pacing decide, because it is a separate prepaid allowance. A real question (per the new <code>Comserv::Util::AI::TaskTier</code> weak-model and substantive-prompt lists, moved out of <code>Router.pm</code>) or a question about the current page now qualifies alongside high complexity, while who may <em>use</em> SuperGrok is still the roles-only <code>route_override_allowed</code> check, which fails closed. (2) <em>Page debugging.</em> <code>Chat.pm</code> recognises "how does this page behave" questions (<code>is_page_debug_prompt</code>), bounds the route with <code>canonical_route</code>, and attaches a fixed server-side code window for the route from <code>CodeRead->page_extra_specs</code>; nothing is derived from page or template text. Source is only attached when <code>page_debug_source_allowed</code> passes (agent allowed for a code agent <em>and</em> <code>CodeRead->authorized</code>). (3) <em>Code Guard.</em> <code>CodeRead->authorized</code> is now enforced inside <code>prepare_turn</code>, <code>follow_up_context</code> and <code>related_context</code>, so a caller bug cannot bypass it; config and credential paths (<code>config/</code>, <code>keys/</code>, <code>.ssh</code>, <code>secrets</code>, <code>*.conf|cnf|ini|env|yml|yaml</code>, key/password/token names) are never readable even by an authorized reader.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> The OpenRouter cap was being read as a global "no paid model" signal and silently downgraded users who still had SuperGrok quota. Separately, <code>_is_privileged</code> read <code>grep { ... } @$roles ? 1 : 0</code>, which grepped the literal <code>1</code>/<code>0</code> and returned false for every role list — the privilege check was dead. Model chains also treated an absent chain key as an error although <code>load()</code> fills it from the Perl default; the zero-priced free-model list is now aliased from <code>Util::AI::FreeModel</code> instead of copied.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>lib/Comserv/Model/AI2/{Router,Chat,CodeRead,ModelPick,UsageMonitor}.pm</code>, <code>lib/Comserv/Model/AI/Usage.pm</code>, <code>lib/Comserv/Util/AI/{ModelChains,FreeModel,TaskTier}.pm</code>, <code>root/ai/widget.tt</code>.</p>
</div>
